    kind: work_item  # c038
    title: "usage_contexts metadata HTTP-method key is 'methods' (list) but spec §9.914/§9.928 documents 'http_method' (string); 0/8 carry the documented key -> consumer KeyError"  # c038
    status: todo_hard  # c038
    priority: 1  # c038
    parent:  # c038
    tags:  # c038
    - dogfood  # c038
    - dogfood_tranche_05  # c038
    isbefore: []  # c038
    duplicate_of: []  # c038
    not_duplicate_of: []  # c038
    pr_ref:  # c038
    description: "Spec §9.914/§9.928 documents the route HTTP method under metadata.http_method as a single string ('http_method': 'GET'); the substrate emits metadata.methods as a list ('methods': ['GET']). 0/8 usage_contexts carry the documented http_method key. Substrate metadata (route): {'args': ['/health','_health'], 'methods': ['GET'], 'receiver': 'Route', 'route_path': '/health', 'view_name': '_health'} — key is methods, value is a list. Spec example §914: 'metadata': {'http_method': 'GET', 'route_path': '/users'}; route_path matches the spec (8/8), only the method key drifts. Probe: usage_contexts with metadata.http_method (spec key) = 0; with metadata.methods = 8. Fresh tracker run reproduces identically. Consequence: an LLM/dev consumer following the documented schema to read a route's HTTP verb does metadata['http_method'] and gets a KeyError/None on every route; the verb actually lives under a differently-named, differently-typed key (methods list). This is a 🟩-marked (done) surface in the spec."  # c038
    fields: {}  # c038
- op: discuss  # 20d5
